** How does IHHT differ from real altitude training in the mountains?


In altitude training the overall exposure time is longer. The desired effects of Altitude training is often the
Impact on Heamoglobin levels and Oxydative Capacity. This effect is archived throgh hypoxic conditioning to altitude
and takes several weeks of exposure.

IHHT/IHT applies short burst of moderate hypoxia with low Frequency (minutes to hours), intermittent (switching),
isocapnic (no CO2 interference), normobaric (at sea level)

IHT/IHHT has stacking effects. Due to intermittece the short more intense exposure times lead to recurring body adaptions
that add on to each other. Additionally this change might have additional benefits on Mitochondrial quality control.

IHT/IHHT can be easyer and faster adjusted to the individual than altitude.
This requires experience and precise monitoring. ReOxy archives this automatically through SRT.

