** How long, often, and intensively should IHHT be conducted?

Interval Hypoxia-Hyperoxia Training (IHHT) with the ReOxy is carried out in sessions where patients alternately breathe
hypoxic (low-oxygen) and hyperoxic (high-oxygen) air. These 30 - 50 minute sessions consist of intervals lasting several
minutes (typically between 3 and 10 minutes) and can be repeated multiple times a day or week depending on the
doctor’s prescription. In most clinical settings the Therapy gets applied 2-5 times a week for 3-5 weeks.


The effectiveness of IHHT/IHT depends on several key factors in the Treatment Protocol

- Intensity of Hypoxia
  This is determined by the fraction of inspired oxygen (FiO2) and can be measured by blood oxygen saturation (SpO2).
  - Low Frequeny Moderate hypoxia (10-16% inspired oxygen) and a low number of cycles (3-15 episodes per day) often lead to positive
    effects.
  - Servere (2-9% inspired oxygen) and or High Frequency hypoxia (48-2400 episodes/day) can increasingly cause damage.
- Phasse Duration of Hypoxia Hyperoxia/normoxia
  The length of hypoxic hyperoxic or normoxic phases
- Number of Cycles
  The number of switches between hypoxia and hyperoxia during a session
- Session Duration
  Length of a single Session
- Pattern of IHHT Application
  For example, consecutive days versus alternating days.
- Total Duration of the Protocol
  The overall length of the IHHT program.
- CO2 levels
  The Treatment should be conducted under nomal CO2 levels (isocapnic) and should not impact them significantly.
  Varying CO2 Levels during the treatment impact our chemoreceptors, can lead to hyper or hypoventilation
  and negate some effects.
- Flowrate
  The Amount of airflow the device provides impacts the Breath-Work of the patient and his breathing response
  to the hypoxic stimuli.  
- Arousal state during treatment
  The arousal state of the patient impacts several key parameters. The therapy often gets refered to as relaxing
  and sleep inducing. However a resting/sleeping state might not always be desireable as it decreases certrain effects.


** What to look out for in IHHT devices?

The following criteria are met by the ReOxy and apply to the medical application of IHHT for desease treatment.

- Medical Certification
  For the Treatment of deseases the device should be medically certified by a notified body.
- Intendet Use
  The device should have a defined medical intendet use. Usually found in the User Manual.
- Service and Maintainance
  The provider should offer regular maintainance.
- Device Specifications
  - Protocol
    - Under look under (link to How long, often, and intensively should IHHT be conducted?) if the device meets the required
      parameters
  - Filtration
    There are diffrent filration techniques used by IHHT devices, ask the manufacturer what technology they use.
    Some technologies are more prone to error and require regular replacement of internal sensors.
  - Aid for Individual Dose adjustment
    Most devices offer so called hypoxic tests. They range from breath holding tests to simple puls oximetry
    up to multi staged tests. They work diffrently, if they determine the dose the device should have reseach
    behind it to back up the effectiveness as this will significally impact the Treatment Protocol.
  - Sensor Tech
    The Internal oxygen sensor can either work chemically or electically. Chemical sensors have to be checked
    regularly and have to be replaced in regular intervals to ensure accuracy. While the Electrical Sensors are
    more Expensive they just require a regular check up.
- Training
  Does the Provider offer Training and introduction by Medical Professionals?

